A copy of the Apache License, Version 2.0 is included as LICENSE in this
directory, as required by Section 4(a) of that License.

Modifications made to the ported content, per Section 4(b):
  - Ported from Go to JavaScript (ES modules).
  - Regex syntax adapted from Go's RE2 engine to ECMAScript: Go named
    groups `(?P<n>...)` converted to ECMAScript named groups
    `(?<n>...)`; Go's `\A`/`\z` absolute anchors converted to `^`/`$`;
    Go's inline, rest-of-pattern `(?i)` case-insensitivity toggle detected,
    stripped, and reapplied as a whole-pattern `i` flag on the compiled
    RegExp (a documented, accepted approximation for the couple of rules
    where `(?i)` appears after a case-sensitive literal prefix).
  - The two rules built via Go's `fmt.Sprintf()` over shared string
    constants (aws-access-key-id, aws-secret-access-key) were expanded by
    substituting those constants into their final literal pattern form.
  - Go's `MustCompileWithoutWordPrefix()` / `MustCompileWithBoundaries()`
    helper wrapping (word-boundary guards around the secret-bearing group)
    was reimplemented directly in the generated pattern source.

This directory contains ONLY the ported rule data (rules.js, allow-rules.js)
plus this NOTICE and the Apache LICENSE it requires. The scanning engine
that consumes this data (file walking, extra non-Trivy rules, allow-rule
application, report shaping) is original UBEL code and lives outside this
directory — see ../../secrets.js — and is licensed under UBEL's own terms,
not Apache-2.0. Only the contents of this directory are Apache-2.0.
